# Checkpoint slimming and scratch cleanup of 2026-11-01

Why: C: was 100 % full (4.1 GB free), bev_fusion/temp held 18 GB, bev_fusion/runs 11 GB of resume checkpoints. Mirko: "slim the checkpoints to the necessary ones, also delete unneeded data or cached information or outdated information". This record is the list of what was done (written by hand from the logs of the session, not generated by a tool).

## Checkpoints: $TOT
Rule: a run is slimmed only if it has the done flag and its last checkpoint is the configured end step (unfinished, stopped or old runs keep their resume checkpoints; none was found). Slim form = what the pinned code snapshot of an OLD run still loads: the Adam moments (2 x the parameters) are emptied, param_groups and RNG stay, slim = True. Weights, EMA, step and cfg were compared tensor by tensor with the original before the swap. Then bev_adapter.load_run (the evaluation's own load path, under the run's pinned code in runs/<name>/code) had to load the new file, else the full file was put back (no failure occurred). Only then the full copy and the older checkpoints were deleted. A slim checkpoint evaluates and warm-starts (init_from), it cannot resume training. Runs whose checkpoints live in D:/bev_fusion_ckpts (t2_*, t3_*) were slimmed in place. The D: copies of t1_r0, t1_r3_combined, t1_r4_soa (full size) were left as the backup of the slimmed C: files.

| run | before MB | after MB | checkpoints before |
|---|---|---|---|
EOF
